WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:02.980
<i>I'm Hasegawa Kouta.</i>

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.660
<i>I'm a 17 year old high school
second-year who loves Sanrio.</i>

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.150
<i>When we all went to Sanrio Puroland together,</i>

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.490
<i>and I saw the Miracle Gift Parade, I realized</i>

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.810
<i>that I want to sparkle.</i>

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.540
<i>Because of that, the five of us decided</i>

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.230
<i>to put on a musical at the school festival.</i>

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.090
<i>We made money with part-time jobs.</i>

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.050
<i>And now we're all going
on a training camp trip.</i>

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.070
It's really the ocean!

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.340
What's the not-real ocean, then?

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.410
Is all of this reserved for us?!

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:47.140
A private beach, totally impressive!

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.490
Okay then, we're all here because we need to—

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.940
Woohoo!

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.060
Hey!

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.390
We didn't come here to play around.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.530
This is a training camp
for the five of us to deal

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.580
with the difficult tasks for the musical!

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.530
Let's do our best in the training camp!

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.370
Lemme go!

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.970
Let me go swimming!

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.360
The Boys' Vacation!

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.780
<i>Hase, let's go to the beach!</i>

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.900
Sorry, Macchi, I'm already
at the beach with everyone.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.920
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.110
<i>Tsucchi was even looking forward to it!</i>

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.850
I'm really sorry you guys!

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.160
<i>Wha— that's not—</i>

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.000
<i>I'm...</i>

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.300
<i>...really at the beach, right?</i>

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.770
What a mess.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.450
I didn't think there'd be so few ideas.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.360
Don't you have anything?

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.060
Huh?

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.980
Isn't England like the center for musicals?

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.100
If anything, America is...

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.770
This really is rough when we're all amateurs.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.820
We already knew that from the get-go.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.990
Besides, the point of this training
camp was to take our time

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.440
and concentrate our energy on this.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.160
Anything goes.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.320
So if you have any ideas...

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.580
I-I do.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.340
That's right, you were the one who
came up with the idea for this musical.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.140
Well...

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.100
Sh-Should it really be a musical?

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:14.400
I mean, it could be a comical or
magical kind of like a musical?

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.600
Or something... kind of... like that...

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:22.520
Okay...

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:24.240
Strip.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.200
Just strip already!

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.390
What is it? What kind of
swimsuit are you wearing?

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.880
Show me! Just show it to me!

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.690
No, I'm not wearing any yet!

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:35.920
Hey, what are you—

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.130
You strip, too.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.450
Hey, we're trying to talk right now.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.860
I can't talk anymore.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.800
We can't do anything just shut up in here.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.820
But...

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.290
Um...

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:58.400
You all go play. I'll think
enough for all of us.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:01.610
Understood.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.070
Strip.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:10.090
This training camp is also
intended to strengthen our unity.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.880
There's no way we could leave
one of our friends behind.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.630
First, we refresh our minds and bodies.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.800
Let's go enjoy the ocean guys!

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.050
Yeah!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.130
Y-Yeah!

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.970
Woohoo!

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.310
<b>It's supposed to be Purin, 
more or less.</b>

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.400
Hey, where's Yuu?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:44.150
I saw him heading towards the house.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:45.420
Thanks.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.010
Hey, Yuu.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.490
Where are you?

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.720
Y-Yuu?

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.320
What's wrong?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:07.410
Um, I wanted to thank you...

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.070
You know, when you said what you did earlier,

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.140
you made things less tense.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.280
Thank me?

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:16.660
Yeah.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:17.600
Then.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.290
Y-Yuu?

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.220
Hey... it's okay, right?

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:25.390
If you want to thank me... here!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.130
I'll leave this to you!

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.630
Hey, Yuu?!

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.350
That's right,

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:44.560
I took out my contacts so
I could get in the water.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:48.180
I realized it when the onion
really stung my eyes.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.060
Contacts?

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.150
I figured it was about time everyone would
be getting hungry and I was in a rush.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:01.500
We hadn't really decided anything,
but you're going to cook for us?

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:04.580
All men dream of training camp food.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.260
Training camp food?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:09.600
All men dream of a stockpot!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.970
All men dream of a natural gas rice cooker!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:21.310
I was totally jealous of the sports club
when I saw them using these things.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.540
W-Were you?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.700
Come on now, we have
to hurry or we won't make it.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.100
You help too, Kouta.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.040
But what are you making?

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.870
When you think of a man's summer,
only curry comes to mind!

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.200
The spice really gives it a kick.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.740
I don't really need it to have a kick!

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:40.290
I'd rather it was mild!

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.290
Thank you for the food!

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.210
More please.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.340
More please.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.860
No need to rush.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.090
You prefer mild, right?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:57.800
Yeah.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.570
We've refreshed ourselves now,

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.810
so we're going to really focus
on training this afternoon.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.980
We still haven't decided what
kind of story we're going to do,

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.840
but basic physical abilities
are also essential.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:11.530
So, do you want seconds?

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.170
I do.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.120
You don't need to overdo it, Kouta.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.820
Don't take it easy on him, Shunsuke.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:32.710
But...

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.750
The drama club often trains as well.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:40.030
Abdominal muscles strengthened
for speaking are indispensable.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:46.040
Breathing is important when
you're going to shoot an arrow.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.340
You could say I strengthened them naturally.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.370
What are you doing?

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.050
Well, they might answer my prayers.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.450
You think so?

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.630
No, it won't.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.010
But it could...

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.500
Come on now.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.250
Her ribbon is red, A, B, C, D, E!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.840
Her ribbon is red, A, B, C, D, E!

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:15.550
Kiki and Lala are sparkling, F, G, H, I, J!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.380
Kiki and Lala are sparkling, F, G, H, I, J!

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:21.660
I'm exhausted.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.960
Hey, we still have training left.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.230
Now, now.

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.350
Come on, if you give it your best a bit longer,

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.640
it'll be dinner time.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:29.730
Dinner!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.100
So, what's on the menu?

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:31.810
Curry.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.060
Wha?!

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.480
We just had that for lunch!

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.700
I made too much of it.
Same with the rice and roux.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.230
There's only five of us, you know.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:44.870
But it's more delicious
if you make a bunch of it.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.340
We're eating curry again?

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:48.050
Isn't the curry more delicious
on the second day?

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.520
It's still the same day!

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:52.730
Maybe if you change up the
ingredients in the curry—

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:53.530
Oh, a crab.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.700
Get it!

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.960
It's really coming down out there.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.410
Use current location information

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.410
Current Weather...Rainy

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.410
Humidity (%): 92 
Precipitation (mm/1): 86

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.980
How's the weather?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.210
It'll be raining till morning.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.410
But all that's left to do is sleep.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:37.700
You're wrong about that.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.730
That's right, night time at training camp means

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.950
games or pillow fights!

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.200
Pillow fights?

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.120
Pillows fly all over the room!

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.590
By a poltergeist?

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:50.810
Not even.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.100
That's not what I meant,

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.810
we need to use every spare
moment for the musical and—

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:01.500
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.030
Who turned out the lights?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.450
No, this is...

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.390
A blackout?

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:06.800
Calm down, everyone!

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:08.910
You have to remain calm.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:20.080
That's... not the kind of thing
you use in an emergency.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.160
So, what should we do now?

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.090
Shouldn't we just wait and see?

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.640
Like this in the dark?

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.190
The breaker wasn't tripped either,

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:33.020
so there's nothing amateurs like us can do.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:36.890
All right.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:38.520
Let's go to bed.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.900
Moving around carelessly
in the dark is dangerous.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.740
All we can do is go to bed.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:47.570
Even though we just ate dinner?

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.510
I can't fall asleep this early.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:51.980
We can compensate for it.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:53.160
Compensate?

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.790
By waking up tomorrow at 4 AM!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:57.560
4 AM?

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:59.000
I couldn't get up!

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:03.010
If we go sleep, we'll get 8 hours
of sleep. It's not a problem.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.430
That's not the way you compensate
for something like that though.

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:13.720
Ow...

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.260
Be careful where you're stepping.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.900
This isn't a school field trip.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:21.350
But doesn't this feel better than being alone?

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:22.390
Besides...

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:23.980
Pillow fight!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:25.990
We're not doing it.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:27.450
They're not going to fly?

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.830
They don't fly.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.170
But we're finally spending a night together,

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.660
seems kind of a waste not to do anything.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.340
Just hurry up and go to sleep.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:40.460
But even if we don't do anything, doesn't
it seem like something might happen?

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:41.430
Like what?

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.300
A murder.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.560
M-Murder?

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:53.140
Isn't this typical?

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:56.140
It's pitch black in the mansion.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.460
The storm outside makes escape impossible.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:04.650
These are the conditions
for fearsome serial killers.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.950
Th-There's nothing like that.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:10.190
After all, there's only the five of us here.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:13.780
You sure?

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.280
Are there really only five of us?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.190
What do you mean?

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.910
Lost in the darkness...

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.420
It's not us but a sixth person!

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:27.850
No way!

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.220
There is not.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.460
I told you.

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:32.350
Come on, go to sleep.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.880
Jeez, such buzzkills.

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:37.810
Oh well,

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:39.830
I'm going to sleep, too.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.120
Wait, guys?!

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:03.060
<i>How can everyone sleep
normally in a situation like this?</i>

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:04.840
<i>The sixth person...</i>

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.200
<i>There's no such thing!</i>

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.590
<i>I better go to sleep, too.</i>

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.730
Shunsuke, Shunsuke!

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:16.180
Did you hear a strange sound just now?

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:17.600
Hey.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.310
I didn't.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.490
But...

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:22.340
Just go to sleep.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.460
There it is again! It's a strange noise!

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:29.860
Shunsuke! Shunsuke!

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:34.820
Want me to put you to sleep permanently?

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.330
I-I'm sorry!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.370
Hey, Shunsuke—

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.590
Hey, President.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:51.760
Hey...

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.470
H-He's alive, right?

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.410
Hey, Yuu.

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:02.970
My Melody!

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:05.170
I'm not My Melody... Hey!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:13.920
Thanks for walking to the bathroom with me.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.050
You're a second-year.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:19.540
Aren't you scared, Ryo?

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:24.000
Well, about the sixth person.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.170
There's no such thing.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:30.790
What was that?

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:32.270
You heard it too, right?

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:33.780
Right?

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.910
Ryo, are you...?

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.590
I-I'm not scared or anything!

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:47.150
Besides, no one would normally sneak
into a place with five guys anyway.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:49.550
But if they weren't normal...

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.240
If it's not a normal person then...
what if it's a ghost or something?

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:59.340
Ghost?

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.330
A ghost? Is that all?

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.050
Huh?

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:04.840
Then we have no problem.

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.920
N-No, we still have a problem!

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:10.760
A ghost is someone who's already dead, right?

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:12.130
It's not that scary.

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.060
It is though?

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.490
Nobody is afraid of them in England.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.140
Really? In England?

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:22.900
Could that be the pillow fight?

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:26.660
Wait, a pillow fight isn't some
paranormal phenomenon!

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.530
Th-There really is a sixth person!

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.630
Sorry, did I wake you?

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:53.340
Y-Yuu?

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:59.030
You were eating curry by yourself?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:03.680
No way, I just thought of an idea
for a new secret ingredient.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.910
I figured I'd surprise everyone
tomorrow morning.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:08.690
So we're having curry tomorrow, too.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:10.270
What are you doing?

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.810
I told you all to go straight to bed, didn't I?

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.340
Why are you all awake?

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.970
Was that you, Ryo?

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:17.910
No.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:23.130
A-Anyway, why are you making such
delicious smells in the middle of the night?

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:24.780
Yuu, give me some.

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:25.550
Hey!

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:28.080
I'm so hungry I won't be able to sleep now.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.330
But it's not good for your body
to eat unnecessarily at night.

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.340
I kind of want some, too.

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.450
Yeah, me, too.

00:18:34.450 --> 00:18:34.990
Hey!

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.620
I-I'll make a special exception!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.330
I want a large portion, Yuu!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.460
I just want a normal one.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.280
I want a normal—

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.520
No, never mind, I'll do a large portion.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.030
All right, coming right up.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:57.040
<i>We had some trouble on our first day,</i>

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:08.150
<i>but after that, there were no major problems,</i>

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:13.680
<i>and our fun time passed
by in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>But...</i>

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.990
<i>The training camp ends today, huh?</i>

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:33.150
<i>But... we never decided on
what to do for the musical.</i>

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:36.970
<i>We could've at least figured out the story.</i>

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.210
Hey, Yuu, what's that?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:57.170
Kouta likes sparklers?

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.260
This is...

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.170
I figured I might find some hints.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:02.050
We couldn't come up with any
ideas just thinking about it, right?

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:05.810
With everyone enjoying
themselves naturally like this,

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:08.690
I wondered if we couldn't
use some of it in the musical.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.180
So that's what it was.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:15.100
I wondered what you were writing.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:18.180
What're you two doing?

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:20.110
I think Yuu should do it.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:23.320
The musical's story.

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.200
Let's have Yuu write it!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.570
What're you on about now?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.460
You're the one always watching us, aren't you?

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:36.560
With the meals, you realized about
when we would be getting hungry.

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:39.240
That's because I'm always doing that at home.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:43.230
Yuu will definitely come up with
a story that suits us the best!

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:43.860
Right?

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:45.900
But I'm a total amateur.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:48.260
We all are though.

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.730
You guys...

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:55.730
You better not complain about
the story I come up with.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:00.750
It'll be fine. We have Ryo, too.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:01.730
Huh? Me?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.770
You're from the center of musicals, right?

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:06.010
I told you, that's America.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.100
You're quite knowledgeable
since you're a library assistant.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.740
Well... I am a library assistant.

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:13.540
<i>That's right.</i>

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.660
<i>With the five of us,</i>

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:18.480
<i>we'll manage our first musical somehow.</i>

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:22.090
<i>If we all put our heads together,</i>

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:24.720
<i>I'm sure of it!</i>

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.400
I'm home!

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:09.010
I missed you, my son!

00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:09.810
Huh?

00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:13.430
Dad! When did you get back?

00:23:13.430 --> 00:23:17.120
Be glad! I actually have some really good news.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.560
No way...

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.890
Next Episode

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:39.380
Next time, <i>"Dream Galaxy, Compassion Planet"</i>.
